# __APP_NAME__

A Winia application generated by Winia Forge.

## Desktop

```bash
cargo run
```

## Android

`[android].abis` lists every ABI that goes into the APK; the generated project defaults to
`arm64-v8a` and `x86_64`, so one APK runs on both real devices and emulators. Each ABI needs
its Rust target installed (`rustup target add aarch64-linux-android x86_64-linux-android`).

```bash
winia build --target android
adb install -r android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
```

`winia build --abi arm64-v8a` narrows the build to a single ABI when a smaller APK is wanted.

`winia build` locates the NDK, injects the linker / `CC` / `AR` environment, copies the
`.so` into `android/app/src/main/jniLibs/<abi>/`, verifies 16 KB alignment, and runs the
Gradle wrapper. It needs `ANDROID_NDK` (or an NDK under the Android SDK) and LLVM libclang
for bindgen.

The generated Android project uses GameActivity and the Vulkan backend, matching the Skia
prebuilt archive that includes `svg`.
